{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778975479167,"sessionID":"ses_1cccce2a6ffeGfzsOIz23No5hc","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"webfetch","callID":"call_jCwWMMhky9iXW0ZG9tLUQXKU","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/search?q=%22endochondral%20ossification%22&ontology=go","format":"text","timeout":30},"output":"{\"response\":{\"docs\":[{\"iri\":\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0001958\",\"ontology_name\":\"go\",\"ontology_prefix\":\"GO\",\"short_form\":\"GO_0001958\",\"description\":[\"Replacement ossification wherein bone tissue replaces cartilage.\"],\"label\":\"endochondral ossification\",\"obo_id\":\"GO:0001958\",\"type\":\"class\"},{\"iri\":\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0035993\",\"ontology_name\":\"go\",\"ontology_prefix\":\"GO\",\"short_form\":\"GO_0035993\",\"description\":[\"The process whose specific outcome is the progression of the deltoid tuberosity over time, from its formation to the mature structure. The deltoid tuberosity is the region on the shaft of the humerus to which the deltoid muscle attaches. The deltoid tuberosity develops through endochondral ossification in a two-phase process; an initiating tendon-dependent phase, and a muscle-dependent growth phase.\"],\"label\":\"deltoid tuberosity development\",\"obo_id\":\"GO:0035993\",\"type\":\"class\"},{\"iri\":\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0010363\",\"ontology_name\":\"go\",\"ontology_prefix\":\"GO\",\"short_form\":\"UBERON_0010363\",\"description\":[\"A skeletal element that has the potential to participate in endochondral ossification, and may participate in intramembranous ossification.\"],\"label\":\"endochondral element\",\"obo_id\":\"UBERON:0010363\",\"type\":\"class\",\"exact_synonyms\":[\"endochondral replacement element\"]},{\"iri\":\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004763\",\"ontology_name\":\"go\",\"ontology_prefix\":\"GO\",\"short_form\":\"UBERON_0004763\",\"description\":[\"Replacement bone tissue that forms within cartilage[VSAO, modified].\"],\"label\":\"endochondral bone tissue\",\"obo_id\":\"UBERON:0004763\",\"type\":\"class\"},{\"iri\":\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002241\",\"ontology_name\":\"go\",\"related_synonyms\":[\"calvarium\",\"neurocranium\"],\"ontology_prefix\":\"GO\",\"short_form\":\"UBERON_0002241\",\"description\":[\"Endoskeletal elements that encase the brain, nose, inner ear[cjm]. that part of the neurocranium formed by endochondral ossification and comprising the bones of the base of the skull[TFD].\"],\"label\":\"chondrocranium\",\"obo_id\":\"UBERON:0002241\",\"type\":\"class\"},{\"iri\":\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0010843\",\"ontology_name\":\"go\",\"ontology_prefix\":\"GO\",\"short_form\":\"UBERON_0010843\",\"description\":[\"A cartilaginous condensation that has the potential to develop into a clavicle.\"],\"label\":\"clavicle cartilage element\",\"obo_id\":\"UBERON:0010843\",\"type\":\"class\"},{\"iri\":\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0010844\",\"ontology_name\":\"go\",\"ontology_prefix\":\"GO\",\"short_form\":\"UBERON_0010844\",\"description\":[\"A pre-cartilage condensation that has the potential to develop into a clavicle.\"],\"label\":\"clavicle pre-cartilage condensation\",\"obo_id\":\"UBERON:0010844\",\"type\":\"class\"},{\"iri\":\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001703\",\"ontology_name\":\"go\",\"related_synonyms\":[\"brain case\",\"brain pan\",\"braincase\"],\"ontology_prefix\":\"GO\",\"short_form\":\"UBERON_0001703\",\"description\":[\"Subdivision of skeletal system that surrounds and protects the brain. Includes the skull base, sensory capsules and the central part of the skull roof.\"],\"label\":\"neurocranium\",\"obo_id\":\"UBERON:0001703\",\"type\":\"class\",\"exact_synonyms\":[\"brain box\"]},{\"iri\":\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002514\",\"ontology_name\":\"go\",\"related_synonyms\":[\"intramembranous bones\",\"membrane bone\"],\"ontology_prefix\":\"GO\",\"short_form\":\"UBERON_0002514\",\"descript